WEBVTT

00:02.990 --> 00:03.690
Ow, hot!

00:04.720 --> 00:05.690
How is it?

00:05.690 --> 00:06.810
Looks good!

00:06.810 --> 00:07.870
Hot, hot, hot...

00:16.180 --> 00:17.860
The fish is ready!

00:22.060 --> 00:23.330
What's wrong, Suzuki?

00:23.330 --> 00:26.410
No... the tofu's crushed...

00:30.540 --> 00:31.210
Oh!

00:31.210 --> 00:32.460
This looks delicious!

00:32.460 --> 00:33.510
Indeed.

00:39.040 --> 00:40.230
Delicious!

00:41.500 --> 00:43.420
Food that's freshly cooked always tastes better.

00:44.810 --> 00:46.810
It really is delicious!

00:46.810 --> 00:49.270
Maybe we should ask Gouta-kun to help out again tomorrow!

00:49.270 --> 00:51.110
Sure, if it's just fish.

00:51.110 --> 00:52.730
The miso soup is delicious too!

00:52.730 --> 00:53.550
Yeah!

00:54.270 --> 00:56.990
Sora-chan, you've fully recovered now.

00:57.840 --> 01:01.450
I... made all of you so worried...

01:01.450 --> 01:03.350
Your health comes first, Sora-chan!

01:04.330 --> 01:06.110
Really, I'm glad.

01:11.340 --> 01:13.110
Aww, she's blushing!

03:03.750 --> 03:06.980
I see... Kuroda-kun hasn't returned...

03:06.980 --> 03:07.690
Yeah.

03:10.050 --> 03:12.820
It'd be nice if we could all graduate together...

03:12.820 --> 03:16.200
I think he probably feels the same way.

03:16.200 --> 03:17.410
Yeah...

03:22.740 --> 03:23.870
Good morning!

03:23.870 --> 03:25.920
Sorry for making you all worry about me.

03:25.920 --> 03:27.960
Catching a cold in this heat...

03:27.960 --> 03:29.380
Just what did you do?

03:29.380 --> 03:31.800
The heat in Tokyo seems somewhat different...

03:31.800 --> 03:32.530
Yes...

03:32.530 --> 03:35.340
it's almost like someone gradually strangling the life out of you...

03:35.340 --> 03:37.330
That kind of heat is scary!

03:38.150 --> 03:40.850
I hope Kuroda-kun comes back...

03:40.850 --> 03:44.770
It's not an easy thing to overcome failure.

03:44.770 --> 03:46.060
Is that so?

03:46.060 --> 03:49.330
I think Kuroda-kun will return, though.

03:49.880 --> 03:51.780
Life is like a marathon.

03:52.610 --> 03:53.640
What do you mean?

03:54.190 --> 03:55.800
It's no use trying to speed things up.

03:56.420 --> 03:57.660
I see.

03:57.660 --> 03:58.830
You're right.

03:59.470 --> 04:01.020
Ah, it's Kawada!

04:04.940 --> 04:06.040
Good morning.

04:06.290 --> 04:07.900
Good morning!

04:08.940 --> 04:11.410
Well then, let's begin today's lecture.

04:12.180 --> 04:16.920
Today we will be discussing ten cases of actual negotiations with clients.

04:14.120 --> 04:14.960
Earlier...

04:16.580 --> 04:17.420
What I said earlier...

04:17.420 --> 04:19.260
In our first case,

04:17.420 --> 04:19.260
It was from Fune-san.

04:19.260 --> 04:24.930
we have a fourth-grade boy who has a dog that bites everything and anything...

04:19.690 --> 04:20.730
I see!

04:26.280 --> 04:28.770
Kuroda-kun hasn't come today either...

04:31.100 --> 04:34.190
You know, maybe... he'd find it easier to come out if he has a good reason to?

04:34.190 --> 04:36.050
What kind of reason?

04:43.730 --> 04:45.240
Instructor Morishita!

04:45.240 --> 04:46.490
What's wrong?

04:47.450 --> 04:48.850
Sorry for interrupting the lecture!

04:50.160 --> 04:55.000
There's been an emergency request from the Kujuukuri Town Hall to the Magic Department!

04:58.370 --> 04:59.180
Here...

04:59.750 --> 05:00.470
Thank you.

05:07.170 --> 05:10.600
It must be a crucial case if they're asking for the trainees to participate, right?

05:11.130 --> 05:12.330
That's right.

05:15.190 --> 05:18.560
Everyone, today's lecture has been cancelled.

05:20.920 --> 05:24.070
A large amount of dolphins have been stranded at Kujuukurihama.

05:24.070 --> 05:28.370
The Magic Department has decided to request the help of the trainees as well.

05:28.370 --> 05:30.280
Stranded dolphins...

05:30.280 --> 05:32.700
I've never taken such a lesson before.

05:32.700 --> 05:33.790
Owata-kun!

05:33.790 --> 05:35.250
Refrain from whispering!

05:36.590 --> 05:37.830
Everyone, calm down.

05:38.510 --> 05:42.000
This is a good chance for us to experience what group magic for disaster relief feels like.

05:42.000 --> 05:43.300
Instructor Morishita.

05:43.300 --> 05:45.550
Please make me a copy of the map of the scene.

05:45.550 --> 05:46.350
My pleasure!

05:51.680 --> 05:52.510
Suzuki-san.

05:52.510 --> 05:53.400
Yes?

05:53.930 --> 05:55.390
Are you feeling better now?

05:55.390 --> 05:57.000
Yes, completely!

05:57.730 --> 05:59.840
If anything happens, inform me right away.

06:00.390 --> 06:03.270
All the instructors will watch over you.

06:03.270 --> 06:05.670
Yes, thank you very much!

06:08.370 --> 06:12.850
This morning, a large number of dolphins were stranded at Chiba Prefecture's Kujuukurihama.

06:13.490 --> 06:18.290
Presently, local volunteers and a rescue team have begun relief measures; however,

06:18.290 --> 06:22.020
because of their large numbers, the dolphins remain in an extremely dangerous situation.

06:24.510 --> 06:25.440
Who could that be?

06:26.500 --> 06:27.560
Hello?

06:28.040 --> 06:29.760
Oh, Sora-chan?

06:29.760 --> 06:30.530
What's wrong?

06:33.300 --> 06:34.500
Stranded dolphins?!

06:36.530 --> 06:37.330
I see.

06:38.620 --> 06:39.320
Okay,

06:39.910 --> 06:41.600
I'll go to the afternoon job alone.

06:41.600 --> 06:44.060
Make sure you save the dolphins, all right?

06:45.970 --> 06:46.810
It's fine.

06:46.820 --> 06:48.110
You should go too, Gouta-kun.

06:48.110 --> 06:52.130
Chances to use group spells don't come by often, after all.

06:54.180 --> 06:55.110
Yes!

06:55.110 --> 06:56.860
You're a mage too, aren't you?

06:58.380 --> 06:59.080
All right.

06:59.480 --> 07:00.180
Bye!

07:02.180 --> 07:04.960
Gouta-kun and the others are going to use a group spell?

07:04.960 --> 07:05.730
Yes.

07:06.580 --> 07:10.940
For all we know, it may become a boost to his magic!

07:20.200 --> 07:23.310
You're sure the train is faster than the car?

07:23.310 --> 07:25.630
The city streets are jam-packed at noon, you know.

07:28.730 --> 07:30.510
Everything seems so calm...

07:31.100 --> 07:33.140
It's the calm before the storm.

07:35.950 --> 07:40.380
I've seen stranded dolphins on TV before.

07:40.630 --> 07:41.760
What was it like?

07:43.200 --> 07:45.450
Since they can't tell where the sea stops and the beach begins...

07:45.450 --> 07:49.270
they come onto shore when they were actually intending to swim along the coast.

07:50.060 --> 07:56.200
I've only seen videos of turtle hatchlings heading towards the sea as fast as they can.

07:58.420 --> 08:00.590
Apparently, sometimes when they swim out of their territory,

08:00.590 --> 08:02.590
their sense of height becomes distorted.

08:03.070 --> 08:07.370
They may think they're swimming up when they're actually swimming deeper into the sea.

08:12.450 --> 08:15.060
I wonder if I can use my magic properly...

08:15.060 --> 08:16.150
Don't worry!

08:16.150 --> 08:17.730
You can do this!

08:17.730 --> 08:19.190
I hope so...

08:21.250 --> 08:25.570
I can't imagine what rescuing stranded dolphins is like...

08:25.570 --> 08:27.400
This may be a lot tougher than we thought.

08:28.060 --> 08:29.220
Even you, Hono-chan?

08:29.730 --> 08:30.790
It'll be fine!

08:30.790 --> 08:32.880
Morishita-sensei's with us!

08:38.670 --> 08:39.590
Morishita...

08:40.350 --> 08:42.420
is surprisingly weak when it comes to the real thing.

08:58.410 --> 09:01.900
I've never been afraid of surfing tournaments before.

09:01.900 --> 09:03.110
Yeah!

09:03.110 --> 09:07.750
Rather than worry about it, we should try to learn as much as we can when we get there!

09:08.520 --> 09:10.470
Surfing tournament?

09:11.150 --> 09:13.520
So Midorikawa-kun's dream is to become a surfer?

09:14.460 --> 09:15.470
My dream?

09:17.200 --> 09:18.650
Dream, huh...

09:19.120 --> 09:21.750
I've heard about Kuroda Kouji's dream before.

09:21.750 --> 09:23.110
What?

09:23.790 --> 09:26.420
He was boasting about it.

09:26.990 --> 09:29.380
"I'm interested in national defense."

09:29.950 --> 09:35.140
"I think Japan's national security is ten years behind other countries."

09:35.140 --> 09:38.770
"That's why I intend to change all that."

09:38.770 --> 09:40.690
Kuroda-kun's awesome!

09:40.690 --> 09:42.980
If you ask me, it's just a pie in the sky.

09:42.980 --> 09:44.820
Do you have a dream, Hono-chan?

09:46.830 --> 09:47.910
I...

09:48.620 --> 09:49.610
want to be a diplomat.

09:49.610 --> 09:51.920
That's so careerwoman-like!

09:52.530 --> 09:53.370
I...

09:53.940 --> 09:58.150
want Japan to cherish its relationship with the other Asian countries.

09:58.700 --> 10:01.660
Why can't we get along with our neighbors?

10:02.290 --> 10:04.080
Japan and the world...?

10:04.490 --> 10:06.710
I've never thought about it before...

10:06.710 --> 10:08.100
What's your dream, Suzuki?

10:09.010 --> 10:12.510
It's been my dream from when I was young to be a mage.

10:12.510 --> 10:13.200
I see.

10:14.530 --> 10:15.960
What about Hiyo-chan?

10:19.730 --> 10:23.610
My dream is to open a magic company in Nagasaki.

10:24.290 --> 10:25.770
You can definitely do it!

10:25.770 --> 10:26.980
Thank you!

10:30.740 --> 10:34.190
We haven't heard Midorikawa-kun talk about his dream yet.

10:34.190 --> 10:35.630
My dream...

10:36.360 --> 10:38.620
I want to know what Gouta-kun's dream is.

10:40.640 --> 10:45.570
It's my dream to become a professional surfer and go around the seas of the world.

10:46.170 --> 10:47.700
The seas of the world...

10:48.150 --> 10:50.080
We're going to the sea now too!

10:50.080 --> 10:52.500
Kujuukuri has great waves!

10:52.500 --> 10:53.590
I knew it.

10:53.170 --> 10:54.110
The waves.

11:09.850 --> 11:10.700
Toukin?

11:11.150 --> 11:12.660
Huh, that doesn't make sense.

11:11.150 --> 11:17.360
He misread the 金 part of the name of the station. He read 東金 as Toukin, but as you can read in the sign, it's Tougane.

11:12.950 --> 11:15.360
The sea is nine kilometers away from Tougane station.

11:15.360 --> 11:17.410
Come, let's take a taxi there.

11:17.410 --> 11:20.200
Hey, we came all the way here by train...

11:20.200 --> 11:22.200
Ah, don't use that one...

11:22.200 --> 11:24.070
Where do you want to go?

11:23.070 --> 11:26.860
Argh, but, hey, you know, listen...

11:26.210 --> 11:28.290
We're here as requested by the Magic Department.

11:28.290 --> 11:30.160
Please take us to Katakai Beach.

11:30.160 --> 11:30.850
Roger!

11:35.650 --> 11:36.790
The dolphins, right?

11:36.790 --> 11:37.520
Yes.

11:37.920 --> 11:39.920
I've been driving so many people there.

11:39.920 --> 11:40.970
Is that so?

11:41.530 --> 11:42.360
Yes...

11:42.760 --> 11:46.650
it seems like the relief workers are short-handed.

11:47.220 --> 11:49.060
Mages should be going there as well.

11:49.060 --> 11:50.460
I feel sorry for them...

11:52.440 --> 11:54.770
I hope all the dolphins can be helped...

11:54.770 --> 11:55.980
Yes!

11:55.980 --> 11:59.120
I'm sure they still have a lot of things they want to do too!

12:05.090 --> 12:06.740
Give it your best shot, mages!

12:26.500 --> 12:27.370
Gouta-kun.

12:28.150 --> 12:29.150
Gouta-kun!

12:30.410 --> 12:31.140
Let's go!

12:33.040 --> 12:35.210
Come on, the dolphins are waiting for us!

12:37.150 --> 12:39.020
Excuse me... let us pass, please.

12:39.020 --> 12:40.080
Excuse me!

12:40.480 --> 12:41.400
Please...

12:41.770 --> 12:43.070
Excuse me!

12:43.070 --> 12:44.330
I'm coming through!

12:45.670 --> 12:46.610
Who are you?

12:46.610 --> 12:48.570
We're here as requested by the Magic Department.

12:48.570 --> 12:49.730
We're trainees.

12:50.360 --> 12:51.570
We've been waiting!

12:51.570 --> 12:53.740
The rescue team can't handle this by themselves...

12:53.740 --> 12:55.620
Hey, over here!

12:55.030 --> 12:57.660
These are the instructions for the dolphin rescue.

12:59.040 --> 13:01.290
Please read this and use your magic.

13:03.830 --> 13:04.660
What about practice?

13:05.070 --> 13:07.440
You may not be able to do it properly at first, but...

13:07.830 --> 13:10.680
please pick up the technique as you carry out your magic.

13:12.180 --> 13:14.300
Good luck to all you mages.

13:15.010 --> 13:16.760
The southern sea floor is getting weaker!

13:16.760 --> 13:17.720
Understood!

13:17.720 --> 13:19.430
Get Yamamoto's team there!

13:19.430 --> 13:20.130
Yes, sir!

13:20.800 --> 13:21.520
Bye!

13:26.010 --> 13:26.990
I see.

13:27.410 --> 13:28.440
Simply put...

13:28.440 --> 13:33.280
We have to cover the dolphins with seawater, lift up the seawater with the dolphins inside and return them to the sea.

13:33.280 --> 13:37.550
We have to bring them as far out to the sea as possible so they don't get stranded again.

13:38.050 --> 13:39.790
I wonder if I can do that...

13:40.670 --> 13:42.840
The poor dolphins...

13:43.710 --> 13:45.160
Yamabuki Hiyori!

13:45.160 --> 13:49.000
If you must cry, then make it tears of joy AFTER you rescue the dolphins!

13:49.000 --> 13:50.130
Okay.

14:10.930 --> 14:13.730
I've never cast a combination of spells like this before...

14:25.840 --> 14:26.620
What's wrong?

14:26.620 --> 14:28.410
I can't seem to... hold the seawater properly...

14:28.410 --> 14:31.420
Then try imagining a piece of paper or a cloth wrapper!

14:31.420 --> 14:32.300
I see!

14:41.040 --> 14:41.910
Thank you!

14:42.340 --> 14:43.330
It's working!

14:43.850 --> 14:45.050
You're welcome.

14:46.860 --> 14:47.830
Why...

14:48.320 --> 14:49.480
I saw it on the news.

14:49.920 --> 14:51.940
I'm sort of a mage too, so...

14:54.770 --> 14:56.860
Come on, move them to the coast!

14:56.860 --> 14:57.770
All right!

15:07.270 --> 15:08.140
It's not working...

15:08.700 --> 15:10.740
At this rate, the dolphins will...

15:12.570 --> 15:13.410
Hiyo-chan!

15:13.410 --> 15:14.670
Take a deep breath!

15:14.670 --> 15:15.540
What?

15:15.540 --> 15:16.630
Sora-chan?

15:16.630 --> 15:18.650
Don't be so nervous!

15:19.070 --> 15:20.700
You have to relax!

15:21.790 --> 15:22.510
Okay!

15:37.280 --> 15:38.820
GO!

15:39.560 --> 15:41.260
Hiyo-chan, that's amazing!

15:42.740 --> 15:44.370
I have to do my best too!

15:57.450 --> 15:59.000
Move... move...

16:05.440 --> 16:06.670
Dammit...

16:31.880 --> 16:34.000
Are you tired, nii-chan?

16:35.960 --> 16:40.740
Eat this, feel better, and rescue the dolphins!

16:43.790 --> 16:44.790
All right.

16:52.780 --> 16:53.760
It's delicious!

16:53.760 --> 16:55.150
Thank you, baa-chan!

17:09.560 --> 17:10.250
Hey!

17:10.620 --> 17:12.860
Those who are not mages will hinder the rescue!

17:12.860 --> 17:14.350
Leave this area!

17:35.980 --> 17:37.100
Are you giving up?

17:37.710 --> 17:38.520
Shut up!

17:39.410 --> 17:41.850
And you call yourself a man?!

17:41.850 --> 17:42.730
What?!

17:44.450 --> 17:45.860
Gouta-kun can do it.

17:47.000 --> 17:48.150
You can definitely do it!

17:49.010 --> 17:50.650
I'll lend you my power.

18:03.280 --> 18:04.710
Don't weaken your powers!

18:05.180 --> 18:06.670
Let's lift them up now!

18:12.570 --> 18:14.100
Good going, Gota-kun!!

18:26.250 --> 18:28.440
Gouta-kun, you did it!

18:28.950 --> 18:30.890
This is your true power.

18:34.930 --> 18:36.780
Go for it, Gouta!

18:37.390 --> 18:38.190
Oh...

18:38.190 --> 18:39.190
Me too...

19:02.440 --> 19:03.170
Hey,

19:03.600 --> 19:05.050
Midorikawa Gouta.

19:05.740 --> 19:06.880
I saw...

19:07.650 --> 19:08.930
your magic.

19:11.840 --> 19:12.700
Kuroda?

19:14.000 --> 19:14.710
You...

19:15.490 --> 19:18.520
Looks like you might overtake me if I'm too careless.

19:18.520 --> 19:19.560
Yeah, I guess.

19:19.560 --> 19:22.940
Thanks for coming to see me the other day.

19:22.940 --> 19:23.720
No prob.

19:30.360 --> 19:32.030
We're mages.

19:32.680 --> 19:33.380
Yeah.

19:34.280 --> 19:35.460
We are.

19:51.840 --> 19:52.650
Welcome back.

19:54.420 --> 19:55.170
I'm back.

20:05.250 --> 20:06.690
Do you want seconds?

20:06.690 --> 20:08.110
Ah, no.

20:08.110 --> 20:09.000
I've had enough.

20:09.480 --> 20:10.440
Sora-chan?

20:10.440 --> 20:12.450
I'm full!

20:12.450 --> 20:13.610
I want seconds!

20:13.610 --> 20:14.620
All right, all right.

20:15.200 --> 20:17.280
I saw the evening news.

20:17.810 --> 20:19.700
The trainees did a good job, huh?

20:19.700 --> 20:20.550
Yes!

20:22.170 --> 20:25.840
Gouta-kun's magic was really awesome!

20:26.450 --> 20:28.500
I already heard it from Gouta-kun.

20:28.500 --> 20:30.200
Thank you, Sora-chan!

20:30.930 --> 20:35.800
I remembered Hara-sensei lending me his powers during my training...

20:36.450 --> 20:37.480
I see, I see!

20:38.380 --> 20:40.080
I was really carried away!

20:40.690 --> 20:46.490
I felt like Gouta-kun would drift away from magic if he couldn't use his powers back then, so...

20:48.190 --> 20:49.380
Sorry...

20:49.810 --> 20:51.440
I dozed off...

20:51.440 --> 20:53.070
My, my, you were asleep?

20:53.070 --> 20:55.070
You must be tired, really.

20:55.070 --> 20:56.820
Well done!

21:01.680 --> 21:03.870
Is Gouta all right?

21:03.870 --> 21:05.540
He's fast asleep.

21:05.540 --> 21:07.890
Reminded me how good it is to be young.

21:12.250 --> 21:15.930
Looking at Gouta reminds me of Haruka.

21:16.600 --> 21:19.300
No news about Haruka-chan since then?

21:19.300 --> 21:20.220
None at all.

21:20.830 --> 21:21.680
I see...

21:22.850 --> 21:24.810
She's a pretty stubborn one too, after all...

21:25.640 --> 21:26.640
Is she already 18?

21:29.670 --> 21:30.930
I see...

23:05.850 --> 23:07.570
Do you know Enoshima?

23:07.570 --> 23:09.690
Do you know anything about the Esca?

23:07.570 --> 23:11.300
The Enoshima Esca (short for escalator) is a 106m long and 46m tall escalator.

23:09.690 --> 23:11.300
Fujimi restaurant...

23:13.050 --> 23:14.620
Next episode: First Love

23:15.400 --> 23:19.580
Calling it a car romance sounds so embarrassing...
